# Go standards

The authoritative rules live in `.agent/rules/go-standards.md`, relative to the repository
root. Read that file before writing or reviewing Go code here. This stub deliberately keeps
no copy of the rules, so the file is the only place they are maintained.

It covers error wrapping and `Err` sentinel naming, context and mutex handling, function
length and cyclomatic complexity limits, the dot-import and import-order policy, where unit
tests must live (`test/unit/<area>/`, never beside `controllers/**/internal`), and banned
dependencies.

